=begin pod :kind("Type") :subkind("class") :category("basic")

=TITLE class RakuAST::Type::Subset

=SUBTITLE Represent a type without any additional features

    class RakuAST::Type::Subset { }

The C<RakuAST::Type::Subset> class represents an C<enum> specification.

=head2 Object introspection

C<RakuAST::Type::Subset> object is typically created when parsing
Raku Programming Language code.  So most developers will only need to
know how to introspect the objects created.

=head3 is-coercive

=begin code :preamble<my $subset>
say $subset.is-coercive;  # True or False
=end code

The C<is-coercive> method returns whether the "of" type is coercive.

=head3 name

=begin code :preamble<my $subset>
say $subset.name;  # RakuAST::Name.from-identifier("Foo")
=end code

Returns the C<L<RakuAST::Name>|/type/RakuAST/Name> object of this
C<RakuAST::Type::Subset> object.

=head3 of

=begin code :preamble<my $subset>
say $subset.of;  # RakuAST::Type::Simple.from-identifier("Int")
=end code

Returns the C<RakuAST::Type>> object of this C<RakuAST::Type::Subset>
to which the C<enum> B<values> are constrained.

=head3 scope

=begin code :preamble<my $subset>
say $subset.scope;  # my
=end code

Returns the scope of the C<RakuAST::Type::Subset> object as a string.
Usually "our", but can also be "my" or "anon".

=head3 traits

=begin code :preamble<my $subset>
dd $subset.traits;  # ()
=end code

Returns a (possibly empty) list of L<C<RakuAST::Trait>|/Type/RakuAST/Trait>
object that were applied to the C<enum>.

=head3 where

=begin code :preamble<my $subset>
dd $subset.where;  # * %% 2
=end code

Returns the L<C<RakuAST::Expression>|/Type/RakuAST/Expression> object
that represents the names and values of this C<enum>.

=head2 Object creation

There are is only one way to reate a C<RakuAST::Type::Subset> object.

=head3 new

=begin code
my $subset = RakuAST::Type::Subset.new(
  scope  => "my",
  name   => RakuAST::Name.from-identifier('Foo'),
  of     => RakuAST::Type::Simple.from-identifier('Int'),
  where  => RakuAST::ApplyInfix.new(
    left  => RakuAST::Term::Whatever.new,
    infix => RakuAST::Infix.new('%%'),
    right => RakuAST::IntLiteral.new(2)
  ),
);
dd $subset;  # my Int subset Foo where * %% 2
=end code

Creates a C<RakuAST::Type::Subset> object from the given named arguments.

=item scope - string indicating scope (my/our/anon), default: "our"
=item of - RakuAST::Type object constraining values, default: none
=item name - RakuAST::Name object with the name of the enum, default: ""
=item where - RakuAST::Expression to constrain values with, default: none
=item traits - List of RakuAST::Trait objects, default: none

=end pod
